(r/'qa/PHASE-REVIEW.md').write_text('''# FX13 nonloop phase review\n\nThe actual original 4×32 runtime strip and atlas04 row1 were viewed before generation. The approved semantic order is cracked-earth → ember-rise → flame-peak → ember-residue.\n\n- Cracked earth establishes the dark irregular patch with only two tiny embers.\n- Ember rise ignites the same fissures with three short tongues, two separate smoke wisps and a few sparks.\n- Flame peak changes the tongues' contours and increases their height/width, raises sparks and bends smoke upward. The earth remains fixed.\n- Ember residue removes all tall fire, sparks and smoke, retaining low flickers and scattered hot segments in the original cracks. It remains nonempty and visibly different from the dormant first phase.\n\nThe patch's lower alpha128 contour has at least 98.71% intersection-over-union with frame 1 in the lower Y≥700 diagnostic region. Its bottom contacts are source Y 1134, 1135, 1136 and 1136: a total spread of 2 source pixels, or 0.045 logical pixels. Left/right extents also stay within 2 source pixels. These diagnostics support registration; the entire source and native sequence was also inspected visually. Color-threshold fire area grows from 68 to 11,656 to 63,387 source pixels, then declines to 4,899; this is a diagnostic of actual authored fire growth/decay, not an opacity operation.\n\nThe dark earth is a source-semantic compact motif. It is intentionally opaque inside its ragged silhouette; the exterior is transparent. No unrelated panel, floor, glow cloud, white fringe or magenta backing was found in full-source black/white or six-background native composites. Dark dormant earth has intentionally lower contrast on dark-earth backgrounds. Flame and residue remain distinguishable.\n\nThis is a single pass. There is no renewal or 4→1 seam requirement. All four APNG samples are exactly 1/12 second, num_plays is 1 and the nominal clip is 1/3 second. The final frame is residue; no extra hold frame, 420ms removal or scene lifetime was invented. A future consumer owns final display/removal.\n\nThe parent approved the first pair's static source appearance; final quartet static acceptance was received on 2026-10-20 after full and terminal native review. Browser/live observation has not occurred and no current authored consumer was found. Exact timing and distinct hashes are mechanical proof, not evidence that live playback was watched.\n''')
